omium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331173 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="331173" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/73/331173/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="I7cac60fb0144e090b8decb05d948b2d8d2f8deac" commit="3e1d390ca728bab9865ebad4d22d2499e32ffd25" commit_message="mainboard/skylakes: Configuring gpio PADRSTCFG to PLTRST  With gpio PADRSTCFG set to DEEP &amp; GPIROUTIOXAPIC=1 &amp; PADRSTCFG, causes IRQ storm after S3 resume. GPIOs that fire IRQs via IOAPIC need to get their logic reset over pltrst and hence configuring PADRSTCFG to PLTRST to prevent IRQ strom after S3 resume.  BRANCH=glados BUG=chrome-os-partner:50536 TEST=Build for kunimitsu and Boot on FAB4, no irq storm observed after S3 resume.  Change-Id: I7cac60fb0144e090b8decb05d948b2d8d2f8deac Signed-off-by: Naresh G Solanki &lt;naresh.solanki@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329453 Commit-Ready: Naresh Solanki &lt;naresh.solanki@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Naresh Solanki &lt;naresh.solanki@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331174 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="331174" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/74/331174/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="I87d9c6ac11486decde102b7821f550c2f1a51f1c" commit="6bb8bb7fb355b1b425054e888e5e9c74a39168a3" commit_message="mt8173: mmu: update mmu range before DRAM is initialized.  The DRAM size can not be determined before DRAM is initialized. Since mt8173 only support 2GB and 4GB DRAM models. We map 0x0 to the end of 2GB DRAM address before DRAM is initialized.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=boot to kernel  Change-Id: I87d9c6ac11486decde102b7821f550c2f1a51f1c Signed-off-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327960 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331175 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="331175" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/75/331175/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="I409163fe527e966c184f28d7d9bbc809ae2308ed" commit="dd880a78167c5e55d3f94cf61147a4a37627530d" commit_message="mt8173: detect sdram size at runtime  Remove DRAM_SIZE_MB Kconfig setting and use sdram_size_mb() to detect the DRAM size at runtime.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49427 BRANCH=none TEST=Boot to kernel  Change-Id: I409163fe527e966c184f28d7d9bbc809ae2308ed Signed-off-by: PH Hsu &lt;ph.hsu@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327961 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331176 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="331176" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/76/331176/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="Ifedc9e2dfba5d294297b3a28134997ac1dd38f94" commit="5c222876850a522e516639839740c4f13769e70d" commit_message="mt8173: memlayout: Create DRAM DMA region for NOR flash DMA read.  NOR flash has a hardware limitation that it can't access SRAM region after 4GB mode is enabled. We add a DRAM DMA region after 0x40000000 for NOR flash driver. So that the NOR flash driver can use this region after 4GB mode is enabled.  BRANCH=none BUG=chormoe-os-partner:49229 TEST=Boot to kernel on rev4 w/ 2GB ram and rev3 w/ 4GB ram.      And check /proc/meminfo.  Change-Id: Ifedc9e2dfba5d294297b3a28134997ac1dd38f94 Signed-off-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327962 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331177 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="331177" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/77/331177/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I097b4ee8bff7fddccb117bb75f3281de87761063" commit="84c22c8f5ef0c121ca6d44eff2aa751e8700f0e4" commit_message="Remove SUITE line from tests in multiple suites  These tests included a space in the suite line, which was temporarily confusing the logic to patch up the set of suites based on ATTRIBUTES and SUITE.  BUG=b:27519238 TEST=inspection, script generated these changes  Change-Id: I097b4ee8bff7fddccb117bb75f3281de87761063 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googl